A||||5||mrfixit58||K&N Filter service?||||5||
Z||000000||mrfixit58||03-18-2001||08:20 PM||||Oh, lucky day. I found a K&N filter in one of my parts cars. Problem is, I've never owned one so I don't really have a clue on how to clean it or oil it. If someone with a K&N would be so kind as to tell me how to perform this procedure I would be grateful.<P>Thanks,<BR>Roy||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||03-18-2001||08:51 PM||||1. Pre Clean: Tap te element tp dislodge any larg embedded dirt.  Then brush with a soft bristle brush. ( If complete cleaning is not practical at this time, re-oil the element and reinstall in your vehicle)<P>2. Spray K&N air filter cleaner onto the entire element and let soak for 10 minutes<P>3. Rinse off the element with low pressure water.  Always flush from the clean side to the dirty side. This removes the dirt and does not drive it into the filter<P>4. SQUEEZE OILING: after cleaning the air filter always re-oil before using.  Squeeze K&N air filter oil down into the bottom and along each pleat-only one pass per pleat.  Let the oil wick into the cotton for 20 minutes.  Re-oil any white spotes still sowing.<P>5. Reinstall||||reg||10
Z||000002||mrfiero||03-18-2001||11:46 PM||||It should also be noted that you must let the filter air dry completely before oiling.<P>You need to buy a K&N recharge kit to get the proper cleaner and oil......about $10 or so.  Most parts stores now sell K&N filters, so you can get the kit there.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Slammed Fiero||03-18-2001||11:53 PM||||I was at Mosport this summer watched some guys testing a ferrari challenge car , the guy put his K&N in a Dishwasher , sprayed it with the oil after it came out and off he went. IT was a huge Trailer (semi) 2 cars , ever since then thats how I have cleaned them .. Works awsome!<P>JM||||reg||1
Z||000004||webbee||03-20-2001||12:44 AM||||You can soak the filter in a solution of dishwashing machine soap and get the same effect as putting it in the dishwasher, WITHOUT angering the little lady, bachelors can safely ignore this post.<P>I buy 2 filter elements and clean, dry, oil ahead of the change. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||mrfixit58||03-20-2001||07:24 AM||||Thanks guys,<P>This filter looks like the previous owner bought it, oiled it, installed it, and forgot it. It has so much crud built up it's protruding through the screen. I'll stop by and get a re-charge kit today.<P>Thanks again,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
